ozz-raw-validation-nan: a raw key's time or ratio that is not a number is invalid

RawAnimation::Validate and RawTrack::Validate test a key's time or ratio
by refusing one below 0 or past the end. Both comparisons are false for a
NaN, so a NaN passed: the animation builder then stopped on its own assert
that each time is in range, or, with asserts off, built the NaN into the
runtime clip. The duration's test had the same shape.

Each test now requires the value inside its range, which a NaN never is.

Evidence: zozz's fuzz property, building a raw animation it loaded, stopped
in AnimationBuilder on "Assertion failed: raw_key.time >= 0 && raw_key.time
<= _duration" (ReleaseFast with asserts on); zozz's src/integration_test.zig
loads a raw animation whose key time is NaN and a raw float track whose
keyframe ratio is NaN, and upstream validates both (both measured,
2026-10-31).

diff --git a/libs/ozz/src/animation/offline/raw_animation.cc b/libs/ozz/src/animation/offline/raw_animation.cc
index 9a8e6f0..2ce2704 100644
--- a/libs/ozz/src/animation/offline/raw_animation.cc
+++ b/libs/ozz/src/animation/offline/raw_animation.cc
@@ -44,8 +44,8 @@ static bool ValidateTrack(const typename ozz::vector<_Key>& _track,
   float previous_time = -1.f;
   for (size_t k = 0; k < _track.size(); ++k) {
     const float frame_time = _track[k].time;
-    // Tests frame's time is in range [0:duration].
-    if (frame_time < 0.f || frame_time > _duration) {
+    // Tests frame's time is in range [0:duration]; a NaN is in no range.
+    if (!(frame_time >= 0.f && frame_time <= _duration)) {
       return false;
     }
     // Tests that frames are sorted.
@@ -64,7 +64,7 @@ bool RawAnimation::JointTrack::Validate(float _duration) const {
 }
 
 bool RawAnimation::Validate() const {
-  if (duration <= 0.f) {  // Tests duration is valid.
+  if (!(duration > 0.f)) {  // Tests duration is valid, and not a NaN.
     return false;
   }
   if (tracks.size() > Skeleton::kMaxJoints) {  // Tests number of tracks.
